# Deposit rule: SCRIPTS and RESULT TABLES are versioned; RAW/DERIVED DATA is not.
#
# The repository must stay small enough to be a code record. Everything excluded
# here is either (a) third-party data that must be obtained from its own source
# under its own licence, or (b) large intermediate objects regenerable by the
# scripts that are included. Accession numbers and URLs for every excluded input
# are listed in manuscript/REFERENCES.md and in DEPOSIT.md.

# --- third-party GWAS / eQTL summary statistics (obtain from source) ---
*.gz
# ...but our own derived per-record tables ARE the audit trail and must be tracked.
# They exist because step108/step94d used to keep only summary rows, which is why a
# change of locus partition could not be recomputed. Small (<1 MB each).
!123b_ra_records.tsv.gz
!123c_eqtlgen_hcc_records.tsv.gz
!99d_r13_records.tsv.gz
*.ma
!landi2020_known_loci_grch38.csv
eqtlgen/
hcc/
pheno/
r13/
r13_extracts/
release_extracts/
litaudit/
soskic/
orcs/
icb_bulk/
cancer_extracts_eqtlgen/
hg19ToHg38.over.chain

# --- SMR / plink working trees and binaries (regenerable by build_besd_*.py) ---
bin/
ref/
besd/
besd_meta/
esd/
esd_meta/
smr_out/
smr_meta/
clump_tmp/
clump_tmp_meta/
cache_47/
tmp/
*.vcor
*.vcor1
*.vcor1.vars
*.pgen
*.pvar
*.psam
*.bed
*.bim
*.fam

# --- large single-cell / Seurat objects (regenerable, or third-party) ---
*.rds
*.h5ad
*.h5

# --- node / editor / scratch working trees (never versioned) ---
node_modules/
105a_artifact_work/
.idea/
outputs/

# --- R / Python working state ---
.RData
.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- scratch ---
scratch_*
backup_*
*.tmp

# --- keep: every step*.py / step*.R, every numbered result table (*.tsv, *.csv),
#     figures/*.py, manuscript/*.md, FINDINGS, HANDOFF ---

# build artefacts: regenerate with R CMD build / check, not tracked
*.Rcheck/
review_packet_v9.zip
